A||||6||86SE||Annoying squeeking noise in engine compartment....||||13||
Z||000000||86SE||06-04-2000||11:41 PM||||Its probibly the alternator belt, but it drives me crazy!  It squeels with the radio on, the air on, or any thing else that takes power.  Squeels more at start up, stops when engine gets hot.  Any ideas?  I heard putting brake fluid on the pully will stop the squeeking, is this true??<P>Thanks||||reg||13
Z||000001||GT Bastard||06-05-2000||12:31 AM||||Hell no, just tighten it.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fiasco||06-05-2000||12:39 AM||||Yep.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||06-05-2000||12:39 AM||||Let's see here. Brake fluid eats paint. Belts will sling liquids off. Hmmmm, bad idea?<P>To check to see if it is the belt, spray a little WD-40 on the pulley so that the spray goes under the belt- spray on the top of the belt will not do anything! If the squeaking stops, you found the source of your problem. If your belt is tight and still noisy, WD-40 will actually soften an old hard belt for a little while. (Usually long enough to get through a car auction  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">)||||reg||1
Z||000004||ROB MAC||06-06-2000||12:22 AM||||I think theres a belt dressing made for this purpose. WD is pretty greasy and will crap up the pulleys with that residue it leaves.||||reg||1
Z||000005||86SE||06-06-2000||01:08 AM||||The belt has dust on the left side of it and is black (been rubbed against something).  When it squeels, I can smell burning belt, the belt still has its thickness.||||reg||5
Z||000006||ROB MAC||06-06-2000||11:59 AM||||Clean the pulleys and the belt with hot water and dishsoap. Rinse them well.Dry them and re-install the belt and tighten. If it still sqeaks look at the alternator bearings or the water pump. If your belt is tight it shouldnt sqeak. Is the there anything loose in the area like the battery shield? Mine came loose and rubbed on the pulley making plastic dust and a burnt plastic smell.||||reg||1
